spans.s:
ku-rahasya, n. base secret;
 -rājan, 🞄m. bad king;
 -rājya, n. bad rule.

kuru-kṣetrá, n. plain of Kuru;
 m. 🞄pl. people of Kurukṣetra;
 N. of a country.

kuru-nandana, m. ep. of Arjuna 🞄and of Yudhiṣṭhira;
 -pañcālá, m. pl. the 🞄Kurus and Pañcālas;
 -pāṇḍava, m. du. pl. 🞄descendants of Kuru (i. e. of Dhṛtarāṣṭra) 🞄and of Pāṇḍu.

kūrcá, m. n. bunch of grass;
 n. beard;
 🞄-ka, m. bunch;
 brush;
 beard;
 -tā, f. beardedness;
 🞄-la, a. bearded.

kūrmá, m. (g. ī) tortoise;
 one of the vital 🞄airs which causes the eyes to close;
 -pati, m. 🞄king of the tortoises (who supports the earth).
